  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programme monitoring and evaluation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Assistance to Burundi (HAB) was a &#xA3;18.1m multi-year programme operating from June 2017 to December 2022. The programme operated across three phases. Phase one, from June 2017 to December 2020, focused on food security and malnutrition, data provision, emergency response and migration management. 

Informed by the evolving situation in Burundi, the programme was extended by 2.5 years increasing the budget to &#xA3;18,108,262 from &#xA3;12m, creating phase two which operated from December 2020 to August 2021. In phase two the scope of the programme was broadened to include support for reintegration of returnees from neighbouring countries, primarily from Tanzania, providing short-term food assistance to Burundian and Congolese refugees arriving from Rwanda, support to ICRC for preparedness activities prior to the 2020 elections, and to mitigate the impact of a malaria outbreak (the latter three areas drawing on the programme&#x2019;s existing contingency funding). Additional support was also provided to UNHCR for protection data monitoring and analysis.</narrative>
  </description>
